# Crockpot API — /shopping-list
#
# GET /shopping-list — CROC-021. Behind full AuthMiddleware, same shape
# as /menu. Never writes: a user with no shopping_lists row yet gets 200
# + empty items, no row created. The list itself is a side effect of the
# three /menu/entries write endpoints (CROC-019) — there is no separate
# "regenerate" endpoint to call here, POST/PATCH/DELETE on /menu/entries
# below do that automatically, in the same transaction as the menu write.
#
# CROC-022 (manual items, obtain-toggle, delete-a-generated-item) hasn't
# landed yet, so there's no PATCH /shopping-list/items/:id to tick an
# item obtained — the "tick obtained" step below is a direct SQL UPDATE
# against the dev DB instead. Swap it for the real endpoint once
# CROC-022 ships.
#
# This file creates its own throwaway item + two throwaway recipes
# (both using that item, no unit — "2 eggs"-style) with the ADMIN
# account, so the shopping list actually has something to aggregate.
# Run top-to-bottom: by the end, both recipes are off the menu again and
# the list is back to empty before Cleanup deletes the fixtures.


# ══════════════════════════════════════════
#  Login (ADMIN account)
# ══════════════════════════════════════════

### Login, to get a token for the checks below.
# @name login
POST http://localhost:{{$dotenv PORT}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "REPLACE_WITH_YOUR_REAL_EMAIL",
  "password": "correcthorsebattery"
}

###

@authToken = {{login.response.body.accessToken}}


# ══════════════════════════════════════════
#  Fixtures — one item, two throwaway recipes that both use it
# ══════════════════════════════════════════

### Real item category to hang a throwaway item off.
# @name itemCategory
GET http://localhost:{{$dotenv PORT}}/item-categories

###

@itemCategoryId = {{itemCategory.response.body.$[0].id}}

### Real seeded recipe category.
# @name recipeCategories
GET http://localhost:{{$dotenv PORT}}/recipe-categories

###

@recipeCategoryId = {{recipeCategories.response.body.$[0].id}}

### Throwaway item — no unit involved, keeps this file independent of
### seeded unit ids/order (unit-merging itself is covered by
### internal/repository/shopping_list_test.go's TestRegenerate_* suite).
# @name item
POST http://localhost:{{$dotenv PORT}}/items
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "http-test-shopping-list-item",
  "categoryId": "{{itemCategoryId}}"
}

###

@itemId = {{item.response.body.id}}

### recipeA — serves 4, needs 2x the item.
# @name recipeA
POST http://localhost:{{$dotenv PORT}}/recipes
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "http-test-shopping-list Recipe A",
  "timeInMinutes": 30,
  "serves": 4,
  "instructions": ["Cook it"],
  "categoryIds": ["{{recipeCategoryId}}"],
  "ingredients": [{ "itemId": "{{itemId}}", "quantity": 2 }]
}

###

@recipeAId = {{recipeA.response.body.id}}

### recipeB — serves 4, needs 3x the same item. Combining with recipeA's
### need for the same item into one summed row is the point of this fixture.
# @name recipeB
POST http://localhost:{{$dotenv PORT}}/recipes
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "http-test-shopping-list Recipe B",
  "timeInMinutes": 30,
  "serves": 4,
  "instructions": ["Cook it too"],
  "categoryIds": ["{{recipeCategoryId}}"],
  "ingredients": [{ "itemId": "{{itemId}}", "quantity": 3 }]
}

###

@recipeBId = {{recipeB.response.body.id}}


# ══════════════════════════════════════════
#  GET /shopping-list — before anything's added
# ══════════════════════════════════════════

### ✅ 200 — empty items. No error even if this account has never had a
### shopping list, and no row is created by this GET.
GET http://localhost:{{$dotenv PORT}}/shopping-list
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}

###


# ══════════════════════════════════════════
#  Add recipeA to the menu — shopping list regenerates automatically
# ══════════════════════════════════════════

### ✅ 200 — add recipeA at serves 4 (its own serves — scale 1). Lazily
### creates both the menu row and the shopping list row.
POST http://localhost:{{$dotenv PORT}}/menu/entries
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "recipeId": "{{recipeAId}}",
  "serves": 4
}

###

### ✅ 200 — one item, quantity 2 (recipeA's need, no scaling at serves 4/4).
GET http://localhost:{{$dotenv PORT}}/shopping-list
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}

###


# ══════════════════════════════════════════
#  Add recipeB to the menu — combines into the same row
# ══════════════════════════════════════════

### ✅ 200 — add recipeB at serves 4 too.
POST http://localhost:{{$dotenv PORT}}/menu/entries
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "recipeId": "{{recipeBId}}",
  "serves": 4
}

###

### ✅ 200 — still one item (same item, no unit — same combine key),
### quantity now 5 (recipeA's 2 + recipeB's 3).
GET http://localhost:{{$dotenv PORT}}/shopping-list
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}

###


# ══════════════════════════════════════════
#  Tick it obtained (direct SQL — no PATCH endpoint until CROC-022)
# ══════════════════════════════════════════

### Run this against the dev DB (psql, or your DB GUI of choice),
### substituting the same email used in Login above:
###
###   UPDATE shopping_list_items sli
###   SET obtained = true
###   FROM shopping_lists sl
###   WHERE sli.shopping_list_id = sl.id
###     AND sl.user_id = (SELECT id FROM users WHERE email = 'REPLACE_WITH_YOUR_REAL_EMAIL')
###     AND sli.item_id = (SELECT id FROM items WHERE name = 'http-test-shopping-list-item');


# ══════════════════════════════════════════
#  Bump recipeA's serves — obtained survives, quantity updates
# ══════════════════════════════════════════

### ✅ 200 — double recipeA's serves to 8 (scale becomes 8/4 = 2).
PATCH http://localhost:{{$dotenv PORT}}/menu/entries/{{recipeAId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "serves": 8
}

###

### ✅ 200 — quantity is now 7 (recipeA's 2×2=4 + recipeB's 3), and
### obtained is still true — the SQL UPDATE above must have survived
### this regenerate, not been reset to false.
GET http://localhost:{{$dotenv PORT}}/shopping-list
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}

###


# ══════════════════════════════════════════
#  Remove recipeA from the menu — item shrinks, doesn't disappear
# ══════════════════════════════════════════

### ✅ 200 — remove recipeA.
DELETE http://localhost:{{$dotenv PORT}}/menu/entries/{{recipeAId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}

###

### ✅ 200 — quantity back down to 3 (recipeB's need alone) — same row,
### same id, still obtained true (row updated in place, not
### deleted-and-reinserted).
GET http://localhost:{{$dotenv PORT}}/shopping-list
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}

###


# ══════════════════════════════════════════
#  Remove recipeB too — item disappears entirely
# ══════════════════════════════════════════

### ✅ 200 — remove recipeB. No recipe on the menu needs the item anymore.
DELETE http://localhost:{{$dotenv PORT}}/menu/entries/{{recipeBId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}

###

### ✅ 200 — back to empty items.
GET http://localhost:{{$dotenv PORT}}/shopping-list
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}

###


# ══════════════════════════════════════════
#  Auth
# ══════════════════════════════════════════

### 🚫 401 — no token.
GET http://localhost:{{$dotenv PORT}}/shopping-list

###


# ══════════════════════════════════════════
#  Cleanup
# ══════════════════════════════════════════

### Both recipes are already off the menu (and the shopping list already
### empty) from the walkthrough above, so these are safe to delete directly.
DELETE http://localhost:{{$dotenv PORT}}/recipes/{{recipeAId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}

###

DELETE http://localhost:{{$dotenv PORT}}/recipes/{{recipeBId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}

###

DELETE http://localhost:{{$dotenv PORT}}/items/{{itemId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}

###
